# Turning at eye level must never show the land late (world_view `_in_view`).
# At eye level only the chunks inside the view's wedge are in the scene, and the
# rest are built and PARKED; a turn brings them back on the frame they come into
# view. This stands the staged eye on a city's edge, lets the world finish, and
# shoots consecutive frames while it turns ninety degrees a second: a hole, a
# patch of coarse far land or a model popping in shows as a frame that disagrees
# with its neighbours about the ground near the player.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/far_turn.tour --seed=7 --place=ruined_metropolis --eye=9,6,50 --eye-turn=90 --hour=12 --weather=clear:0
#   (and with --quality=web under --rendering-method gl_compatibility for the web path)
wait 25
shot turn-00
wait 0.2
shot turn-01
wait 0.2
shot turn-02
wait 0.2
shot turn-03
wait 0.2
shot turn-04
wait 0.2
shot turn-05
wait 0.2
shot turn-06
wait 0.2
shot turn-07
